==Personality==
{{Quote|I'm only worthy of my Hero Watch when I'm making other people's lives better. There's a lot riding on what we do, and we'd better not blow it.|Ben 23 on what he learned with [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] in [[Mad World]].<ref name="IaMBW2">''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]''</ref>}}
In a sense, Ben 23 is the same as 10 or 11-year-old Ben Prime was; but without [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Grandpa Max]] to guide him, Ben 23 didn't learn that not all aliens were evil. To fill the void left by the passing of Max, Ben 23 immersed himself in fame and fortune.

Unlike 16-year-old Ben Prime, who tries to not let fame go to his head (as it has cost him dearly several times), Ben 23 has become overconfident, arrogant and reckless because of it. He also did not have the same sense of right and wrong and didn't want to use his Omnitrix to fight crime or help others in need. 

Despite having unlocked around 50 (claimed 90) aliens on his Omnitrix, Ben 23 keeps only 23 in constant use. As stated with his version of [[Feedback (Dimension 23)|Feedback]] (formerly Plug-Man); whenever he introduces a "new alien" to the public, he stops using one of his former ones and puts it into storage in order to stage a comeback sometime later and stoke the demand. He even suggested to Ben Prime on the advice of his agent to form a team-up.

After Ben meets his dimensional counterpart, who sets him on the right path, he begins to act less arrogant and more heroic. At the insistence of Ben Prime, he seeks out the [[Azmuth (Dimension 23)|Azmuth]] of his world in place of Grandpa Max; hoping to make his dimension just as harmonious as Ben Prime's. But he does still retain some of his original personality and enjoys his status as a celebrity; briefly prioritizing his schedule over an interdimensional conflict that might have destroyed his timeline. However, Ben Prime and Azmuth's influence would be effective on him, by rejecting the temptation of joinning the evil Bens amy, choosing instead fighting Eon and protecting Gwen 10 when she needed him the most.

Ben disliked smoothies, much like 11-year-old Ben Prime. Instead, he prefers gyros from a fast-food chain; which he incorporates into a parody of Ben Prime's catchphrase; "it's gyro time!". He did grow somewhat fond of smoothies after his encounter with Ben Prime.

One quirk that sets Ben 23 apart from Ben Prime is his lack of creativity when it comes to naming his aliens. While Ben Prime used clever wordplay (incorporating his aliens physical appearance or abilities) when naming his aliens, Ben 23's names tend to be somewhat simple-minded or lazy. Ben Prime even points out that [[Teeny-Weeny]] is a terrible name for Ben 23's version of [[Nanomech]]. Like Ben Prime in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''/'''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Ben 23 announces his alien's name when transforming.

==History==
===Background===
Max Tennyson died around the time when Ben received the Omnitrix, and he had to teach himself how to use it.<ref name="S23" />

Without Grandpa Max, he lacks the morals of his [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|other counterpart]], and became a rich and famous celebrity over the years.

Ben 23 has movie rights, endorsement deals and uses aliens to make a lot of money. At this point in time, his greatest enemy was the [[Azmuth (Dimension 23)|Intellectuary]].

===Omniverse===
Ben Tennyson first met Ben 23 in ''[[Store 23]];'' after accidentally entering Dimension 23 through [[Blarney T. Hokestar]]'s interdimensional branch of [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]]. Ben 23 proved to be a braggart and show-off who preferred to use his alien forms for publicity instead of altruism, and even gave Ben a few of his tips for crowd-pleasing. Ben 23 eventually discovered that the Intellectuary was his dimension's [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] and would have killed him; if not for Ben Prime's intervention. Ben 23 admitted that due to the death of his Grandpa Max, he ended up using fame and fortune to fill the void Max had left behind. His dimension's Azmuth consoled Ben 23, acknowledging that he had suffered greatly due to Max's death and promised to guide him well in his place.

In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'' and ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Ben 23 becomes involved in [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s plot to destroy all Ben Tennysons across the multiverse. Ben 23 was recruited by [[Professor Paradox]], [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] and [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]], and later joined the fight in which all [[Omnitrix]] wielders were wiped out by the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]]; with the exception of No Watch Ben. Ben 23 was eventually restored when No Watch Ben used [[Clockwork]] to reverse the effects of the Time Bomb and helped defeat Vilgax before being returned to his dimension.

In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]'', Azmuth's Dimension 23 counterpart had Ben Prime mentor Ben 23 on how to be a better hero. After playing video games together, they went after [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]] and [[Subdora]]. They failed to fight them because Ben 23 asks where the cameras are to capture his heroics. Ben Prime explains that he needs to be a hero whether someone will watch or not. They came upon [[Maltruant]] being repaired by [[Dr. Psychobos]]. While battling, due to an accident they were all sent to another dimension. They first thought they blew up [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]] but soon, they discovered they're in [[Mad World|another world]] ruled by an [[Mad Ben|evil version of Ben]].

After hearing that Maltruant needs his key to get his full power back, Ben 23 turned into [[Techno-Bubble]] and upgraded Clockwork. Unfortunately, Maltruant got his key back and froze their Omnitrixes in time rendering them useless. The two Bens were left in the dimension with Dr. Psychobos at the mercy of Mad Ben, who was about to blast the three of them using Perk [[Upchuck]].

In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', he, Ben Prime and Psychobos are enslaved by Mad Ben. While enslaved, he complains about not having celebrity luxuries and suggests they leave while they have the chance. Ben Prime tells him that they need to clean up the mess Mad Ben caused. After escaping, Psychobos repairs their Omnitrixes. They discovered they were synchronized with each other. While fighting, he and Ben Prime argue over the names they give to their heroes.

After defeating Mad Ben, Psychobos revealed that he set their Omnitrixes to blow up. With Ben Prime and Ben 23 using [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]] and [[Brainfrog]] respectively, they fix their Omnitrixes in no time. After attempting another Techno-Bubbled Clockwork combo that fails, [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] appears with Professor Hokestar's dimension-hopping Mr. Smoothy and takes both Bens back home. Before they leave, Ben 23 says that he's only worthy of his Hero Watch when using it to make other people's lives better.

At present, Ben 23 is currently being tutored by his dimension's [[Tetrax Shard (Dimension 23)|Tetrax]], Azmuth and [[SevenSeven (Dimension 23)|SevenSeven]].

==Powers and Abilities==
===Equipment===
[[File:IaMBW1 (521).png|thumb|Hero Watch]]
Ben 23 possesses the [[Hero Watch]]. Through it, he can transform into various aliens and utilize their respective powers.

==Weaknesses==
Ben 23's battle prowess is almost entirely self-taught. Much like Ben Prime when he was younger, Ben 23 tends to fight recklessly in front of people and often has little to no strategy when fighting his enemies.

Ben 23 is afraid of local news weather ladies.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23's Fear.png]]|group = DJW}}

